  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscComm 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "At a patient advisory board meeting, researchers share that they are
    using donated patient samples to test how new drug compounds work on cancer cells.
    You ask how donors\u2019 wishes and privacy are protected in this process. \r\n\r\n<b>Community
    advocates do not play a role in the ethical considerations of research until
    clinical trials begin.</b>\r\n\r\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: "Community advocates can help raise important ethical questions at
    every stage of research\u2014not just during clinical trials. Their involvement
    helps ensure research stays patient-centered and ethically responsible from the
    very beginning. By speaking up early, they help ensure that patient voices, values,
    and protections are considered from the very beginning."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
